From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS=1: Switch 2 draws without a depth buffer are not skipped for a new pipeline

Upstream: Eglantine-Community 7a940ca by rdenno ("vk_pipeline_cache: wait for new pipelines of
Switch 2 draws without depth"). Star Fox drew each font atlas glyph once (no depth, 30 to 672
vertices); a glyph whose pipeline was still building was skipped and stayed blank for the session.

Two places, both off by default (Common::PeSwitch):
- BuiltPipeline: with the asynchronous shaders setting, a Switch 2 draw without a depth buffer
  gets its pending pipeline (the scheduler worker waits for the driver build) instead of nullptr.
  The setting is off on the PS5, so on the console this hunk does nothing.
- CanSkipDraw (0508, EDEN_UP_ASYNC_TRANSLATION): the same rule, so such a draw is never queued on
  the translators nor skipped: it is translated on the GPU thread as with 0508 off, or takes a
  queued job back, or waits for one a worker has started. Draws with a depth buffer bound
  (zeta_enable) are queued and skipped as before, offscreen passes with depth included.

Cost: one GPU-thread translation per new no-depth pipeline (the 0508-off cost for those).
Unset: both functions return exactly what they return today.

Not in TranslationSwitches (vk_pipeline_prep.cpp) on purpose, like EDEN_UP_ASYNC_TRANSLATION: it
changes no SPIR-V or info, so test arms share one prep store.

v2 of the draft: credit corrected (the draft named kraibse; 7a940ca is rdenno's), header
says what the change does on the PS5, comments in the code.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 7edbadb..31213a6 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -2376,6 +2376,13 @@ GraphicsPipeline* PipelineCache::BuiltPipeline(GraphicsPipeline* pipeline) const
     if (draw_state.draw_element_count <= 6) {
         return pipeline;
     }
+    // EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS=1 (Eglantine-Community 7a940ca, rdenno): Switch 2 titles also
+    // draw things they keep once, with more vertices and no depth buffer (font atlas glyphs):
+    // those wait for their pipeline instead of being skipped. Unset: as before.
+    static const bool wait = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS");
+    if (wait && Settings::CurrentProgramIsSwitch2()) {
+        return pipeline;
+    }
     return nullptr;
 }
 
@@ -3047,6 +3054,13 @@ bool PipelineCache::CanSkipDraw() const noexcept {
     if (maxwell3d->regs.zeta_enable) {
         return true;
     }
+    // EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS=1: a Switch 2 draw without a depth buffer can't be skipped, as in
+    // BuiltPipeline, so it is not queued (CanTranslateAsynchronously) and is translated on this
+    // thread as without EDEN_UP_ASYNC_TRANSLATION. Unset: as before.
+    static const bool wait = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS");
+    if (wait && Settings::CurrentProgramIsSwitch2()) {
+        return false;
+    }
     return maxwell3d->draw_manager.draw_state.draw_element_count > 6;
 }
 
